00:24:40.979 --> 00:24:43.281 align:start size:66% position:34%
because then it would
have to be pushing
something else out.

00:24:43.314 --> 00:24:46.985 align:start size:69% position:31%
So it's just not going
to be a large change.

00:24:47.018 --> 00:24:48.553 align:start size:63% position:38%
So where we did find
a difference

00:24:48.586 --> 00:24:50.855 align:start size:75% position:25%
is actually in the shape
of the hippocampus.

00:24:50.888 --> 00:24:52.790 align:start size:72% position:28%
What we saw is
there were some regions

00:24:52.823 --> 00:24:55.627 align:start size:56% position:44%
in the hippocampus
on both sides

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:57.061 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
<i> that appear
 to have changed shape</i>

00:24:57.094 --> 00:24:58.630 size:84% position:58% line:0%
<i> from day one before gaming</i>

00:24:58.663 --> 00:25:00.832 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
<i> to day ten after gaming.</i>

00:25:00.865 --> 00:25:04.068 align:start position:0%
What's really surprising to me
is that as an adult,

00:25:04.101 --> 00:25:05.770 size:84% position:42%
my brain is still changing.

00:25:05.803 --> 00:25:08.273 size:75% position:38%
That makes me wanna take
better care of my brain.

00:25:08.306 --> 00:25:09.407 align:start size:13% position:88%
Yes.

00:25:09.441 --> 00:25:11.309 align:start position:0%
Exercise it more,
'cause it is a thing
that can change.

00:25:11.342 --> 00:25:16.014 align:start position:0%
I'm not just stuck
with what I have now, today.

00:25:16.047 --> 00:25:19.617 align:start size:91% position:9%
I mean, in all of this,
I think that the big takeaway

00:25:19.650 --> 00:25:21.319 align:start size:66% position:34%
is that doing things,

00:25:21.352 --> 00:25:23.755 align:start size:59% position:41%
giving your brain
something to learn,

00:25:23.788 --> 00:25:26.891 align:start size:75% position:25%
something to do,
something to figure out,

00:25:26.924 --> 00:25:28.693 align:start size:66% position:34%
this is what we think
is actually

00:25:28.726 --> 00:25:30.795 align:start size:78% position:22%
keeping your brain sharp.

00:25:30.828 --> 00:25:33.064 align:start position:0%
One way to do that is to keep
watching<i> Mind Field.</i>

00:25:33.097 --> 00:25:34.766 align:start size:50% position:50%
[Craig] Exactly.

00:25:34.799 --> 00:25:36.568
[music playing]

00:25:40.137 --> 00:25:43.741 align:start size:97% position:3%
 [Michael]<i> As our relationship
 with technology becomes
 ever stronger,</i>

00:25:43.774 --> 00:25:47.779
<i>people are bound to worry about
what it will do to our brains.</i>

00:25:47.812 --> 00:25:49.747
Will offloading memory
and computing

00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:52.250
to our machines make us dumber?

00:25:52.283 --> 00:25:56.688
Will our empathy for machines
have negative consequences

00:25:56.721 --> 00:25:59.624
for how we interact
with each other?

00:25:59.657 --> 00:26:02.760
Well, let's look back
to another time

00:26:02.793 --> 00:26:04.762
a new kind of technology
threatened

00:26:04.795 --> 00:26:07.165
to fundamentally
change our brains.

00:26:07.198 --> 00:26:08.766
Two and a half thousand
years ago,

00:26:08.799 --> 00:26:10.802
the Greek philosopher, Socrates,

00:26:10.835 --> 00:26:13.137
worried that
the wide use of writing

00:26:13.170 --> 00:26:15.907
would have a negative impact
on people's minds.

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:19.077
He said that writing would,
to quote his student, Plato,

00:26:19.110 --> 00:26:20.745
"Create forgetfulness,

00:26:20.778 --> 00:26:23.114
because people will
not use their memories.

00:26:23.147 --> 00:26:26.217
They will trust the external
written characters

00:26:26.250 --> 00:26:29.053
and not remember themselves."

00:26:29.086 --> 00:26:30.788
Socrates was right.

00:26:30.821 --> 00:26:33.825
Written language did
fundamentally change our brains.

00:26:33.858 --> 00:26:36.761
But it's also one of
the cornerstones of everything

00:26:36.794 --> 00:26:38.763
modern civilization
has accomplished.

00:26:38.796 --> 00:26:41.866
One of the defining
characteristics of being human

00:26:41.899 --> 00:26:44.736
is that this is not
the boundary of my body,

